oc~watcher_run->proc~handle_manifest_change Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure function command_mode ( settings ) result ( mode ) class ( fpm_build_settings ), intent ( in ) :: settings character ( len = :), allocatable :: mode select type ( s => settings ) type is ( fpm_test_settings ) mode = \"test\" type is ( fpm_run_settings ) mode = \"run\" if ( s % example ) mode = \"run --example\" class default mode = \"build\" end select end function command_mode","tags":"","url":"proc/command_mode.html"},{"title":"print_banner – fpm-watch","text":"public  subroutine print_banner(full_cmdline, settings, w, files, build_secs, roots_count, secs_model, secs_targets, secs_watch) Emit a startup summary and optional configuration/timing records. watch.ready uses normal verbosity; configuration/timings require level 1.\nRead mode from typed settings. Unallocated files count as zero; time\ninputs are seconds and event timing fields are milliseconds. Quiet mode\nsuppresses these records. File-list output is handled separately by the engine. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: full_cmdline class(fpm_build_settings), intent(in) :: settings type( watch_opts_t ), intent(in) :: w type(string_t), intent(in), allocatable :: files (:) real, intent(in) :: build_secs integer, intent(in) :: roots_count real, intent(in) :: secs_model real, intent(in) :: secs_targets real, intent(in) :: secs_watch Calls proc~~print_banner~~CallsGraph proc~print_banner print_banner interface~log_int log_int proc~print_banner->interface~log_int proc~command_mode command_mode proc~print_banner->proc~command_mode proc~ftoa ftoa proc~print_banner->proc~ftoa proc~log_bool log_bool proc~print_banner->proc~log_bool proc~log_event log_event proc~print_banner->proc~log_event proc~log_real log_real proc~print_banner->proc~log_real proc~log_string log_string proc~print_banner->proc~log_string proc~print_configuration print_configuration proc~print_banner->proc~print_configuration str str proc~print_banner->str proc~log_default_int log_default_int interface~log_int->proc~log_default_int proc~log_int64 log_int64 interface~log_int->proc~log_int64 proc~format_log_record format_log_record proc~log_event->proc~format_log_record proc~log_timestamp log_timestamp proc~log_event->proc~log_timestamp proc~log_real->proc~ftoa proc~json_quote json_quote proc~log_string->proc~json_quote proc~print_configuration->proc~log_bool proc~print_configuration->proc~log_event proc~print_configuration->proc~log_real proc~print_configuration->proc~log_string proc~join_csv join_csv proc~print_configuration->proc~join_csv proc~log_strings log_strings proc~print_configuration->proc~log_strings proc~trim_or_default trim_or_default proc~print_configuration->proc~trim_or_default proc~format_log_record->proc~json_quote proc~escape_text escape_text proc~format_log_record->proc~escape_text proc~json_quote->proc~escape_text proc~log_default_int->proc~log_int64 proc~log_strings->proc~json_quote proc~utf8_width utf8_width proc~escape_text->proc~utf8_width Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~print_banner~~CalledByGraph proc~print_banner print_banner proc~rebuild_watch_list rebuild_watch_list proc~rebuild_watch_list->proc~print_banner proc~handle_manifest_change handle_manifest_change proc~handle_manifest_change->proc~rebuild_watch_list proc~watcher_init watcher_t%watcher_init proc~watcher_init->proc~rebuild_watch_list proc~watcher_run watcher_t%watcher_run proc~watcher_run->proc~rebuild_watch_list proc~watcher_run->proc~handle_manifest_change Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine print_banner ( full_cmdline , settings , w , files , build_secs , roots_count , secs_model , secs_targets , secs_watch ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: full_cmdline class ( fpm_build_settings ), intent ( in ) :: settings type ( watch_opts_t ), intent ( in ) :: w type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: files (:) real , intent ( in ) :: build_secs , secs_model , secs_targets , secs_watch integer , intent ( in ) :: roots_count integer :: nfiles character ( len = :), allocatable :: mode , message nfiles = 0 if ( allocated ( files )) nfiles = size ( files ) mode = command_mode ( settings ) message = \"Watching \" // str ( nfiles ) // \" files (\" // mode // \")\" if ( w % once ) then message = message // \"; one-shot\" else message = message // \"; Ctrl+C or touch .fpm-watch.stop to stop\" end if call log_event ( \"info\" , \"watch.ready\" , message , & [ log_int ( \"file_count\" , nfiles ), log_int ( \"root_count\" , roots_count ), & log_string ( \"mode\" , mode ), log_string ( \"command\" , full_cmdline ), log_bool ( \"once\" , w % once )]) call print_configuration ( settings , w ) call log_event ( \"info\" , \"watch.initialized\" , \"Watch list initialized in \" // ftoa ( build_secs ) // \"s\" , & [ log_real ( \"duration_ms\" , build_secs * 100 0.0 ), log_real ( \"model_ms\" , secs_model * 100 0.0 ), & log_real ( \"targets_ms\" , secs_targets * 100 0.0 ), log_real ( \"watch_list_ms\" , secs_watch * 100 0.0 )], verbosity = 1 ) end subroutine print_banner","tags":"","url":"proc/print_banner.html"},{"title":"print_configuration – fpm-watch","text":"public  subroutine print_configuration(settings, w) Report effective model/watch settings at verbosity 1 after startup or refresh. Features are a comma-separated fpm feature string; include/ignore attributes\nare arrays. Poll/debounce fields are milliseconds and rescan is seconds. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class(fpm_build_settings), intent(in) :: settings type( watch_opts_t ), intent(in) :: w Calls proc~~print_configuration~~CallsGraph proc~print_configuration print_configuration proc~join_csv join_csv proc~print_configuration->proc~join_csv proc~log_bool log_bool proc~print_configuration->proc~log_bool proc~log_event log_event proc~print_configuration->proc~log_event proc~log_real log_real proc~print_configuration->proc~log_real proc~log_string log_string proc~print_configuration->proc~log