n_or_test = . true . type is ( fpm_run_settings ) is_run_or_test = . true . end select end function is_run_or_test","tags":"","url":"proc/is_run_or_test.html"},{"title":"resolve_include_file – fpm-watch","text":"private  function resolve_include_file(source_file, include_name, include_dirs) result(path) Resolve an include path, returning a normalized canonical path or an empty string. Existing absolute paths are accepted directly. Relative names are searched\nbeside the source, then in fpm include directories in order, then relative\nto the current working directory. The first existing candidate wins. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: source_file character(len=*), intent(in) :: include_name type(string_t), intent(in), allocatable :: include_dirs (:) Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Calls proc~~resolve_include_file~~CallsGraph proc~resolve_include_file resolve_include_file canon_path canon_path proc~resolve_include_file->canon_path dirname dirname proc~resolve_include_file->dirname exists exists proc~resolve_include_file->exists is_absolute_path is_absolute_path proc~resolve_include_file->is_absolute_path join_path join_path proc~resolve_include_file->join_path proc~normalize_path normalize_path proc~resolve_include_file->proc~normalize_path Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. 