ows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~run_command_and_report~~CalledByGraph proc~run_command_and_report run_command_and_report proc~run_once run_once proc~run_once->proc~run_command_and_report proc~handle_manifest_change handle_manifest_change proc~handle_manifest_change->proc~run_once proc~watcher_init watcher_t%watcher_init proc~watcher_init->proc~run_once proc~watcher_run watcher_t%watcher_run proc~watcher_run->proc~run_once proc~watcher_run->proc~handle_manifest_change Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine run_command_and_report ( cmd , w , exitstat , secs ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: cmd !! Complete serialized command to execute synchronously. type ( watch_opts_t ), intent ( in ) :: w !! Output suppression, cycle generation, and optional output-marker settings. integer , intent ( out ) :: exitstat !! Command status, including 127 when the platform wrapper cannot launch or wait. real , intent ( out ) :: secs !! Elapsed command time in seconds, excluding event formatting and boundary writes. integer ( int64 ) :: rate , t0 , t1 character ( len = :), allocatable :: action , message , level , cycle_id logical :: interrupted , protocol action = \"Command\" if ( index ( cmd , \"fpm build\" ) == 1 ) action = \"Build\" if ( index ( cmd , \"fpm test\" ) == 1 ) action = \"Tests\" if ( index ( cmd , \"fpm run\" ) == 1 ) action = \"Application\" cycle_number = cycle_number + 1_int64 cycle_id = str ( w % restart_count ) // \":\" // str ( cycle_number ) protocol = w % output_markers . and . structured_logging () call log_event ( \"info\" , \"command.started\" , \"Running \" // trim ( cmd ), & [ log_string ( \"command\" , trim ( cmd )), log_bool ( \"silent_fpm\" , w % silent_fpm ), & log_string ( \"cycle_id\" , cycle_id )], force = protocol ) call output_boundary ( \"started\" , cycle_id , protocol ) call system_clock ( count_rate = rate ) if ( rate <= 0_int64 ) rate = 1000_int64 call system_clock ( t0 ) call execute_command ( trim ( cmd ), exitstat , silent = w % silent_fpm , stderr = structured_logging ()) call system_clock ( t1 ) secs = real ( t1 - t0 ) / real ( rate ) interrupted = termination_requested () level = \"info\" message = action // \" succeeded in \" // ftoa ( secs ) // \"s\" if ( exitstat /= 0 ) then level = \"error\" message = action // \" failed (exit \" // str ( exitstat ) // \") after \" // ftoa ( secs ) // \"s\" end if if ( interrupted ) then level = \"info\" message = action // \" interrupted\" end if call log_event ( level , \"command.finished\" , message , & [ log_string ( \"command\" , trim ( cmd )), log_int ( \"exit_code\" , exitstat ), & log_int ( \"duration_ms\" , nint ( secs * 100 0.0 , int64 )), log_bool ( \"interrupted\" , interrupted ), & log_string ( \"cycle_id\" , cycle_id )], force = protocol ) call output_boundary ( \"finished\" , cycle_id , protocol ) end subroutine run_command_and_report","tags":"","url":"proc/run_command_and_report.html"},{"title":"output_boundary – fpm-watch","text":"private  subroutine output_boundary(state, cycle_id, enabled) Flush a stderr boundary marker when the structured output protocol is enabled. The marker follows a blank line and contains the same opaque cycle_id as the command events; stdout and stderr delivery order need not match. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: state character(len=*), intent(in) :: cycle_id logical, intent(in) :: enabled Called by proc~~output_boundary~~CalledByGraph proc~output_boundary output_boundary proc~run_command_and_report run_command_and_report proc~run_command_and_report->proc~output_boundary proc~run_once run_once proc~run_once->proc~run_command_and_report proc~handle_manifest_change handle_manifest_change proc~handle_manifest_change->proc~run_once proc~watcher_init watcher_t%watcher_init proc~watcher_init->proc~run_once proc~watcher_run watcher_t%watcher_run proc~watcher_run->proc~run_once proc~watcher_run->proc~handle_manifest_change Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine output_boundary ( state , cycle_id , enabled ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: state , cycle_id logical , intent ( in ) :: enabled if (. not . enabled ) return write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"\" write ( error_unit , \"(a)\" ) \"@@fpm-watch:\" // state // \":\" // cycle_id // \"@@\" flush ( error_unit ) end subroutine output_boundary","tags":"","url