e's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine begin_raw_output ( redirect , saved ) logical , intent ( in ) :: redirect integer ( c_int ), intent ( out ) :: saved saved = - 1_c_int if (. not . redirect ) return flush ( output_unit ) saved = fpm_watch_redirect_stdout () if ( saved < 0_c_int ) then call log_event ( \"error\" , \"log.redirect_failed\" , \"Cannot redirect fpm output to stderr\" , & [ log_int ( \"os_error\" , int ( - saved ))]) stop 127 end if end subroutine begin_raw_output","tags":"","url":"proc/begin_raw_output.html"},{"title":"end_raw_output – fpm-watch","text":"public  subroutine end_raw_output(saved) Flush raw library output, restore stdout, and close the saved C descriptor. Negative saved values are no-ops. Restoration failure logs an error and\nexits with status 127; a saved descriptor must only be restored once. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=c_int), intent(in) :: saved Calls proc~~end_raw_output~~CallsGraph proc~end_raw_output end_raw_output interface~fpm_watch_restore_stdout fpm_watch_restore_stdout proc~end_raw_output->interface~fpm_watch_restore_stdout interface~log_int log_int proc~end_raw_output->interface~log_int proc~log_event log_event proc~end_raw_output->proc~log_event proc~log_default_int log_default_int interface~log_int->proc~log_default_int proc~log_int64 log_int64 interface~log_int->proc~log_int64 proc~format_log_record format_log_record proc~log_event->proc~format_log_record proc~log_timestamp log_timestamp proc~log_event->proc~log_timestamp proc~escape_text escape_text proc~format_log_record->pr