in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine end_raw_output ( saved ) integer ( c_int ), intent ( in ) :: saved integer ( c_int ) :: error if ( saved < 0_c_int ) return flush ( output_unit ) error = fpm_watch_restore_stdout ( saved ) if ( error /= 0_c_int ) then call log_event ( \"error\" , \"log.redirect_failed\" , \"Cannot restore stdout after fpm model operation\" , & [ log_int ( \"os_error\" , int ( error ))]) stop 127 end if end subroutine end_raw_output","tags":"","url":"proc/end_raw_output.html"},{"title":"execute_command – fpm-watch","text":"public  subroutine execute_command(cmd, exitstat, interrupted, silent, stderr) Wait for a command and return its status while latching handled user interrupts. silent suppresses both output streams and takes precedence over stderr ,\nwhich redirects command stdout to stderr. Both options default to false.\nLaunch/wait errors log command.launch_failed and return 127; ordinary\nfailures preserve the child status. Optional interrupted reports this\ncommand's handled interruption, while termination_requested remains latched. POSIX uses /bin/sh -c and temporarily forwards SIGINT/SIGQUIT/SIGTERM to\nthe immediate child in the foreground process group. Windows launches\nexecutables directly, with a cmd fallback for scripts, and terminates the\nchild's job on console interruption. Normal exits retain background children. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: cmd Serialized command; caller is responsible for quoting individual argv tokens. integer, intent(out) :: exitstat Child/interrupt status, or 127 with a launch-failure event for OS execution errors. logical, intent(out), optional :: interrupted True if the wrapper handled a user interrupt during this command. logical, intent(in), optional :: silent Suppress both command output streams (default false); takes precedence over stderr. logical, intent(in), optional :: stderr Redirect command stdout to stderr (default false). Calls proc~~execute_command~~CallsGraph proc~execute_command execute_command interface~fpm_watch_execute fpm_watch_execute proc~execute_command->interface~fpm_watch_execute interface~log_int log_int proc~execute_command->interface~log_int proc~is_windows is_windows proc~execute_command->proc~is_windows proc~log_event log_event proc~execute_command->proc~log_event proc~log_string log_string proc~execute_command->proc~log_string proc~log_default_int log_default_int interface~log_int->proc~log_default_int proc~log_int64 log_int64 interface~log_int->proc~log_int64 get_os_type get_os_type proc~is_windows->get_os_type proc~format_log_record format_log_record proc~log_event->proc~format_log_record proc~log_timestamp log_timestamp proc~log_event->proc~log_timestamp proc~json_quote json_quote proc~log_string->proc~json_quote proc~format_log_record->proc~json_quote proc~escape_text escape_text proc~format_log_record->proc~escape_text proc~json_quote->proc~escape_text proc~log_default_int->proc~log_int64 proc~utf8_width utf8_width proc~escape_text->proc~utf8_width Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~execute_command~~CalledByGraph proc~execute_command execute_command proc~run_command_and_report run_command_and_report proc~run_command_and_report->proc~execute_command proc~supervisor_loop supervisor_loop proc~supervisor_loop->proc~execute_command proc~maybe_supervise maybe_supervise proc~maybe_supervise->proc~supervisor_loop proc~run_once run_once proc~run_once->proc~run_command_and_report proc~handle_manifest_change handle_manifest_change proc~handle_manifest_change->proc~run_once proc~watcher_init watcher_t%watcher_init proc~watcher_init->proc~run_once proc~watcher_run watcher_t%watcher_run proc~watcher_run->proc~run_once proc~watcher_run->proc~handle_manifest_change Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine execute_command ( cmd , exitstat , interrupted , silent , stderr ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: cmd !! Serialized command; caller is responsible for quoting individual argv tokens. integer , intent ( out ) :: exitstat !! Child/interrupt status, or 127 with a launch-failure event for OS execution errors. logical , intent ( out ), optional :: interrupted !! True if the wrapper handled a user interrupt during this command. logical , intent ( in ), optional :: silent !! Suppress both command output streams (default false); takes precedence over stderr. logical , intent ( in ), optional :: stderr !! Redirect command stdout to stderr (default false). integer ( c_int ) :: status , was_interrupted , launch_error , silent_mode character ( len = :), allocatable :: effective_cmd silent_mode = 0_c_int if ( present ( stderr )) then if ( stderr ) silent_mode = 2_c_int end if if ( present ( silent )) then if ( silent ) silent_mode = 1_c_int end if effective_cmd = trim ( cmd ) if (. not . is_windows ()) then if ( silent_mode == 1_c_int ) effective_cmd = effective_cmd // \" >/dev/null 2>&1\" if ( silent_mode == 2_c_int ) effective_cmd = effective_cmd // \" 1>&2\" end if status = fpm_watch_execute ( effective_cmd // c_null_char , silent_mode , was_interrupted , launch_error ) stop_requested = stop_requested . or . was_interrupted /= 0_c_int if ( present ( interrupted )) interrupted = was_interrupted /= 0_c_int if ( launch_error /= 0_c_int ) then call log_event ( \"error\" , \"command.launch_failed\" , \"Cannot execute command: \" // trim ( cmd ), & [ log_int ( \"os_error\" , int ( launch_error )), log_string ( \"command\" , trim ( cmd ))]) exitstat = 127 else exitstat = int ( status ) end if end subroutine execute_command","tags":"","url":"proc/execute_command.html"},{"title":"fpm_watch_execute – fpm-watch","text":"interface Called by interface~~fpm_watch_execute~~CalledByGraph interface~fpm_watch_execute fpm_watch_execute proc~execute_command execute_command proc~execute_command->interface~fpm_watch_execute proc~run_command_and_report run_command_and_report proc~run_command_and_report->proc~execute_command proc~supervisor_loop supervisor_loop proc~supervisor_loop->proc~execute_command proc~maybe_supervise maybe_supervise proc~maybe_supervise->proc~supervisor_loop proc~run_once run_once proc~run_once->proc~run_command_and_report proc~handle_manifest_change handle_manifest_change proc~handle_manifest_change->proc~run_once proc~watcher_init watcher_t%watcher_init proc~watcher_init->proc~run_once proc~watcher_run watcher_t%watcher_run proc~watcher_run->proc~run_once proc~watcher_run->proc~handle_manifest_change Help Graph Ke