e Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~quote_arg~~CalledByGraph proc~quote_arg quote_arg proc~build_child_command build_child_command proc~build_child_command->proc~quote_arg proc~build_run_command build_run_command proc~build_run_command->proc~quote_arg proc~join_argv join_argv proc~join_argv->proc~quote_arg proc~parse_cli_config parse_cli_config proc~parse_cli_config->proc~quote_arg proc~parse_cli parse_cli proc~parse_cli_config->proc~parse_cli proc~handle_manifest_change handle_manifest_change proc~handle_manifest_change->proc~parse_cli_config proc~parse_cli->proc~join_argv proc~supervisor_loop supervisor_loop proc~supervisor_loop->proc~build_child_command proc~watcher_run watcher_t%watcher_run proc~watcher_run->proc~build_run_command proc~watcher_run->proc~handle_manifest_change proc~maybe_supervise maybe_supervise proc~maybe_supervise->proc~supervisor_loop Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code function quote_arg ( a , windows ) result ( q ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: a logical , intent ( in ), optional :: windows !! Explicit platform selection supports portable serialization checks. character ( len = :), allocatable :: q logical :: use_windows if ( present ( windows )) then use_windows = windows else use_windows = is_windows_os () end if if ( use_windows ) then q = '\"' // escape_quotes_win ( a ) // '\"' else q = \"'\" // escape_quotes_sh ( a ) // \"'\" end if contains !> Escape embedded quotes and trailing backslashes for a double-quoted Windows argv token. pure function escape_quotes_win ( s ) result ( r ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: s character ( len = :), allocatable :: r integer :: j , backslashes r = \"\" backslashes = 0 do j = 1 , len ( s ) if ( s ( j : j ) == achar ( 92 )) then backslashes = backslashes + 1 cycle end if if ( s ( j : j ) == '\"' ) then r = r // repeat ( achar ( 92 ), 2 * backslashes + 1 ) // '\"' else r = r // repeat ( achar ( 92 ), backslashes ) // s ( j : j ) end if backslashes = 0 end do r = r // repeat ( achar ( 92 ), 2 * backslashes ) end function escape_quotes_win !> Replace embedded single quotes with quoted fragments suitable for a POSIX shell. pure function escape_quotes_sh ( s ) result ( r ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: s character ( len = :), allocatable :: r integer :: j r = \"\" do j = 1 , len ( s ) if ( s ( j : j ) == \"'\" ) then r = r // \"'\"\"'\"\"'\" else r = r // s ( j : j ) end if end do end function escape_quotes_sh end function quote_arg","tags":"","url":"proc/quote_arg.html"},{"title":"watch_option_takes_value – fpm-watch","text":"public pure function watch_option_takes_value(a) result(takes_value) Return whether a bare watcher option consumes the following argv token. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: a Return Value logical Ca