rmat\" , \"--watch-fpm\" ) takes_value = . true . case default takes_value = . false . end select end function watch_option_takes_value","tags":"","url":"proc/watch_option_takes_value.html"},{"title":"lower_ascii – fpm-watch","text":"private pure function lower_ascii(s) result(r) Normalize ASCII letters for case-insensitive option values. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: s Return Value character(len=len) Called by proc~~lower_ascii~~CalledByGraph proc~lower_ascii lower_ascii proc~parse_bool parse_bool proc~parse_bool->proc~lower_ascii proc~apply_watch_flag apply_watch_flag proc~apply_watch_flag->proc~parse_bool proc~parse_restart_flags parse_restart_flags proc~parse_restart_flags->proc~parse_bool proc~maybe_supervise maybe_supervise proc~maybe_supervise->proc~parse_restart_flags proc~parse_cli parse_cli proc~parse_cli->proc~apply_watch_flag proc~parse_cli_config parse_cli_config proc~parse_cli_config->proc~parse_cli proc~handle_manifest_change handle_manifest_change proc~handle_manifest_change->proc~parse_cli_config proc~watcher_run watcher_t%watcher_run proc~watcher_run->proc~handle_manifest_change Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure function lower_ascii ( s ) result ( r ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: s character ( len = len ( s )) :: r integer :: k , c , da