is Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine rebuild_watch_list ( self , print_header , watch_changed , refreshed ) class ( watcher_t ), intent ( inout ) :: self logical , intent ( in ) :: print_header !! True for initial setup (fatal errors and startup logging); false for recoverable refreshes. logical , intent ( out ), optional :: watch_changed !! True on a successful refresh if paths or fingerprints differ from the previous snapshot. logical , intent ( out ), optional :: refreshed !! True only after the candidate graph and new fingerprint baseline are accepted. integer ( int64 ) :: rate , t0 , t1 , candidate_manifest_key real :: build_secs_total real :: secs_model , secs_targets , secs_watch integer :: nfiles , nroots real :: dummy_build type ( string_t ), allocatable :: new_files (:) integer ( int64 ), allocatable :: new_mask (:) type ( root_info_t ), allocatable :: new_roots (:) type ( string_t ), allocatable :: old_files (:) integer ( int64 ), allocatable :: old_fp (:) type ( watch_config_t ) :: candidate_cfg type ( error_t ), allocatable :: error if ( present ( watch_changed )) watch_changed = . false . if ( present ( refreshed )) refreshed = . false . candidate_cfg = self % cfg if ( present ( watch_changed )) then if ( allocated ( self % files )) old_files = self % files if ( allocated ( self % fp_prev )) old_fp = self % fp_prev end if call system_clock ( count_rate = rate ) if ( rate <= 0_int64 ) rate = 1000_int64 call system_clock ( t0 ) call compute_watch_files_from_settings ( & settings = candidate_cfg % settings , & w = self % cfg % w , & files = new_files , & file_mask = new_mask , & roots = new_roots , & manifest_key = candidate_manifest_key , & build_secs = dummy_build , & secs_model = secs_model , & secs_targets = secs_targets , & secs_watch = secs_watch , & error = error ) if ( allocated ( error )) then if ( print_header ) then call log_event ( \"error\" , \"watch.init_failed\" , \"Cannot initialize watch list: \" // error % message ) stop 1 end if if ( allocated ( self % last_refresh_error )) then if ( self % last_refresh_error == error % message ) return end if self % last_refresh_error = error % message call log_event ( \"error\" , \"watch.refresh_failed\" , \"Watch list refresh failed: \" // error % message // \"; waiting for edits\" ) return end if if ( allocated ( self % last_refresh_error )) deallocate ( self % last_refresh_error ) call move_alloc ( candidate_cfg % settings , self % cfg % settings ) call move_alloc ( new_files , self % files ) call move_alloc ( new_mask , self % file_mask ) call move_alloc ( new_roots , self % roots ) call self % fm % on_watch_list_built_all ( self % files , self % roots ) self % man_prev = manifest_key_from_files ( self % cfg % settings , self % files ) call init_fingerprints ( self % files , self % fp_prev , self % fp_now , self % changed_idx ) if ( present ( watch_changed )) then watch_changed = watch_state_changed ( old_files , old_fp , self % files , self % fp_prev ) end if if ( present ( refreshed )) refreshed = . true . call system_clock ( t1 ) build_secs_total = real ( t1 - t0 ) / real ( rate ) nfiles = 0 if ( allocated ( self % files )) nfiles = size ( self % files ) nroots = 0 if ( allocated ( self % roots )) nroots = size ( self % roots ) if ( self % cfg % w % debug ) then call log_event ( \"debug\" , \"watch.fingerprint\" , \"Watch graph fingerprint updated\" , & [ log_int ( \"manifest_key\" , self % man_prev ), log_int ( \"root_count\" , nroots ), log_int ( \"file_count\" , nfiles )]) end if if ( print_header ) then call print_banner ( & full_cmdline = self % cfg % fpm_cmdline , & settings = self % cfg % settings , & w = self % cfg % w , & files = self % files , & build_secs = build_secs_total , & roots_count = nroots , & secs_model = secs_model , & secs_targets = secs_targets , & secs_watch = secs_watch ) if ( self % cfg % w % print_files_once ) call print_file_list ( self % files , self % cfg % w ) else call print_configuration ( self % cfg % settings , self % cfg % w ) call log_event ( \"info\" , \"watch.refreshed\" , \"Watch list updated; \" // str ( nfiles ) // \" files\" , & [ log_int ( \"file_count\" , nfiles ), log_real ( \"duration_ms\" , build_secs_total * 100 0.0 )], verbosity = 1 ) if ( self % cfg % w % verbosity >= 2 ) call print_file_list ( self % files , self % cfg % w ) end if end subroutine rebuild_watch_list","tags":"","url":"proc/rebuild_watch_list.html"},{"title":"run_once – fpm-watch","text":"private  subroutine run_once(self, cmd0) Execute one command cycle with before/after plugin callbacks. Plugins may modify the local copy of cmd0 before execution. Store the\nresulting exit status in self%last_exit ; command failure does not stop\nthe engine. Used for startup, edits, manifest refreshes, and rescans. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( watcher_t ), intent(inout) :: self character(len=*), intent(in) :: cmd0 Calls proc~~run_once~~CallsGraph proc~run_once run_once proc~on_after_run_all feature_manager_t%on_after_run_all proc~run_once->proc~on_after_run_all proc~on_before_run_all feature_manager_t%on_before_run_all proc~run_once->proc~on_before_run_all proc~run_command_and_report run_command_and_report proc~run_once->proc~run_command_and_report proc~feat_after_noop watch_feature_t%feat_after_noop proc~on_after_run_all->proc~feat_after_noop proc~feat_before_noop watch_feature_t%feat_before_noop proc~on_before_run_all->proc~feat_before_noop interface~log_int log_int proc~run_command_and_report->interface~log_int proc~execute_command execute_command proc~run_command_and_report->proc~execute