pe Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine filter_watch_files ( files , include , ignore , masks ) type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: files (:) !! Normalized input paths, replaced with the retained subset in the same order. type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: include (:), ignore (:) !! Include and ignore glob lists, respectively; empty/unallocated lists impose no restriction. integer ( int64 ), allocatable , intent ( inout ), optional :: masks (:) !! Aligned file masks; created as zeros if supplied but unallocated, then filtered with files. logical , allocatable :: keep (:) type ( string_t ), allocatable :: out (:) integer ( int64 ), allocatable :: outm (:) integer :: i , k , n , m if (. not . allocated ( files )) return n = size ( files ) allocate ( keep ( n )) do i = 1 , n keep ( i ) = should_keep ( files ( i )% s , include , ignore ) end do m = count ( keep ) allocate ( out ( m )) if ( present ( masks )) then if (. not . allocated ( masks )) then allocate ( masks ( n )) masks = 0_int64 end if allocate ( outm ( m )) end if k = 0 do i = 1 , n if (. not . keep ( i )) cycle k = k + 1 out ( k )% s = files ( i )% s if ( present ( masks )) outm ( k ) = masks ( i ) end do call move_alloc ( out , files ) if ( present ( masks )) call move_alloc ( outm , masks ) deallocate ( keep ) contains !> Retain manifests unconditionally; otherwise require inclusion and no ignore match. logical function should_keep ( path , include_pats , ignore_pats ) result ( ok ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: path type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: include_pats (:), ignore_pats (:) character ( len = :), allocatable :: b b = basename ( trim ( path )) if ( b == \"fpm.toml\" ) then ok = . true . return end if ok = match_include ( path , include_pats ) . and . (. not . match_any ( path , ignore_pats )) end function should_keep !> Test fpm globs after normalizing each nonempty pattern; an absent list matches nothing. logical function match_any ( path , pats ) result ( ok ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: path type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: pats (:) integer :: j character ( len = :), allocatable :: pat ok = . false . if (. not . allocated ( pats )) return do j = 1 , size ( pats ) if ( len_trim ( pats ( j )% s ) == 0 ) cycle pat = normalize_path ( trim ( pats ( j )% s )) if ( glob ( trim ( path ), pat )) then ok = . true . return end if end do end function match_any !> Admit every path for an empty/unallocated include list; otherwise require a glob match. logical function match_include ( path , pats ) result ( ok ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: path type ( string_t ), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: pats (:) if (. not . allocated ( pats )) then ok = . true . return end if if ( size ( pats ) == 0 ) then ok = . true . return end if ok = match_any ( path , pats ) end function match_include end subroutine filter_watch_files","tags":"","url":"proc/filter_watch_files.html"},{"title":"set_low_cpu – fpm-watch","text":"public  subroutine set_low_cpu(flag) Set the process-wide waiting backend: true selects OS sleep, false selects busy waiting. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name logical, intent(in) :: flag Called by proc~~set_low_cpu~~CalledByGraph proc~set_low_cpu set_low_cpu proc~handle_manifest_change handle_manifest_change proc~handle_manifest_change->proc~set_low_cpu proc~parse_restart_flags parse_restart_flags proc~parse_restart_flags->proc~set_low_cpu proc