dges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial logical, private, save :: stop_requested = .false. Latched cancellation request; ordinary child exit codes do not set it. Interfaces interface private  function fpm_watch_execute(command, silent, interrupted, launch_error) result(status) bind(C, name=\"fpm_watch_execute\")) C process wrapper returning child status or 127 for a launch/wait error. command is NUL-terminated. On Windows, silent selects inherited streams:\n0 normal, 1 discard both outputs, 2 redirect stdout to stderr. POSIX ignores\nthis mode because the Fortran wrapper appends shell redirections. interrupted reports handled user interrupts; launch_error holds the OS\nerror code separately from ordinary child failure. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(kind=c_char, len=1), intent(in) :: command (*) NUL-terminated command bytes interoperating with a C string. integer(kind=c_int), value :: silent integer(kind=c_int), intent(out) :: interrupted integer(kind=c_int), intent(out) :: launch_error Return Value integer(kind=c_int) interface private  function fpm_watch_redirect_stdout() result(saved) bind(C, name=\"fpm_watch_redirect_stdout\")) Redirect descriptor 1 to stderr; return a saved stdout descriptor or a negative OS error. Arguments None Return Value integer(kind=c_int) interface private  function fpm_watch_restore_stdout(saved) result(error) bind(C, name=\"fpm_watch_restore_stdout\")) Restore and close a saved stdout descriptor; return zero on success or an OS error. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=c_int), value :: saved Return Value integer(kind=c_int) Functions public  function is_windows () Return whether the current OS is Windows. Arguments None Return Value logical public  function termination_requested () result(requested) Return the process-wide interruption flag latched by prior command executions. Arguments None Return Value logical Subroutines public  subroutine begin_raw_output (redirect, saved) Optionally redirect process stdout to stderr, flushing Fortran output first. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name logical, intent(in) :: redirect integer(kind=c_int), intent(out) :: saved public  subroutine end_raw_output (saved) Flush raw library output, restore stdout, and close the saved C descriptor. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=c_int), intent(in) :: saved public  subroutine execute_command (cmd, exitstat, interrupted, silent, stderr) Wait for a command and return its status while latching handled user interrupts. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: cmd Serialized command; caller is responsible for quoting individual argv tokens. integer, intent(out) :: exitstat Child/interrupt status, or 127 with a launch-failure event for OS execution errors. logical, intent(out), optional :: interrupted True if the wrapper handled a user interrupt during this command. logical, intent(in), optional :: silent Suppress both command output streams (default false); takes precedence over stderr. logical, intent(in), optional :: stderr Redirect command stdout to stderr (default false).","tags":"","url":"module/watch_platform.html"},{"title":"watch_feature_manager – fpm-watch","text":"Feature plugin manager. Provides storage and fan-out calls to a set of enabled feature plugins. The manager owns a growable array of feature objects. Calls are forwarded\nto each feature in insertion order. Uses fpm_strings iso_fortran_env watch_feature_api watch_types module~~watch_feature_manager~~UsesGraph module~watch_feature_manager watch_feature_manager fpm_strings fpm_strings module~watch_feature_manager->fpm_strings iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~watch_feature_manager->iso_fortran_env module~watch_feature_api watch_feature_api module~watch_feature_manager->module~watch