cefile~watch_feature_api.f90 watch_feature_api.f90 sourcefile~watch_feat_stats.f90->sourcefile~watch_feature_api.f90 sourcefile~watch_feat_stats.f90->sourcefile~watch_log.f90 sourcefile~watch_feature_api.f90->sourcefile~watch_types.f90 sourcefile~watch_feature_factory.f90->sourcefile~watch_types.f90 sourcefile~watch_feature_factory.f90->sourcefile~watch_feat_stats.f90 sourcefile~watch_feature_factory.f90->sourcefile~watch_feature_api.f90 sourcefile~watch_feature_factory.f90->sourcefile~watch_feature_manager.f90 sourcefile~watch_feature_factory.f90->sourcefile~watch_log.f90 sourcefile~watch_feature_manager.f90->sourcefile~watch_types.f90 sourcefile~watch_feature_manager.f90->sourcefile~watch_feature_api.f90 sourcefile~watch_fpm_graph.f90->sourcefile~watch_types.f90 sourcefile~watch_fpm_graph.f90->sourcefile~watch_log.f90 sourcefile~watch_fpm_graph.f90->sourcefile~watch_platform.f90 sourcefile~watch_log.f90->sourcefile~watch_types.f90 sourcefile~watch_platform.f90->sourcefile~watch_log.f90 sourcefile~watch_restart.f90 watch_restart.f90 sourcefile~watch_restart.f90->sourcefile~watch_config.f90 sourcefile~watch_restart.f90->sourcefile~watch_log.f90 sourcefile~watch_restart.f90->sourcefile~watch_platform.f90 sourcefile~watch_restart.f90->sourcefile~watch_cmdline.f90 sourcefile~watch_cmdline.f90->sourcefile~watch_platform.f90 sourcefile~watch_cmdsplice.f90->sourcefile~watch_cmdline.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code !> Shared types used throughout `fpm-watch`. !! !! This module defines the configuration records used to pass options and !! `fpm` settings into the engine. module watch_types use , intrinsic :: iso_fortran_env , only : int64 use fpm_strings , only : string_t use fpm_command_line , only : fpm_build_settings implicit none private public watch_opts_t , root_info_t , watch_config_t !> Watcher options assembled from defaults, manifest values, and leading CLI flags. !! !! Timing fields are seconds. Supervisor options are read separately; `restart_count` !! identifies the child generation used in command cycle IDs. !! `set_watch_defaults` initializes format/executable strings and list arrays. type watch_opts_t !> Verbosity level: !! !! - `-1`: quiet (errors and enabled output protocol) !! - `0`: normal !! - `1..2`: more detail integer :: verbosity = 0 !> Output format: text (default), json (JSON Lines), or logfmt. character ( len = :), allocatable :: log_format !> Executable used for build/test/run; defaults to `fpm` on PATH. character ( len = :), allocatable :: fpm_executable !> Enable debug-level records; quiet mode still suppresses them. logical :: debug = . false . !> Seconds between polling scans; normalized to at least 0.05. real :: poll = 0.5 !> Seconds to wait after detecting a change before resampling. real :: debounce = 0.2 !> Optional periodic rescan interval (seconds). `0` disables periodic rescans. real :: rescan = 0.0 !> Run the command once immediately on startup. logical :: run_on_start = . true . !> Request a startup file list; the logger additionally requires verbosity 2. logical :: print_files_once = . false . !> Suppress both command output streams; watcher and model records remain separate. logical :: silent_fpm = . false . !> Bracket command stderr and force cycle events in structured logging only. logical :: output_markers = . false . !> Internal supervisor generation, retained during manifest refresh. integer :: restart_count = 0 !> Also watch dependency project sources (can include paths under build dir). logical :: watch_deps = . false . !> Use OS sleep for waiting to minimize idle CPU usage. logical :: low_cpu = . false . !> Ignore globs, applied after include rules; watched manifests bypass filtering. type ( string_t ), allocatable :: ignore (:) !> Include globs; empty means all eligible files. Watched manifests always remain. type ( string_t ), allocatable :: include (:) !> Watcher-plugin names, distinct from fpm build features. type ( string_t ), allocatable :: enabled_features (:) !> Run once (init + optional run-on-start) and exit (CI-friendly). logical :: once = . false . end type watch_opts_t !> Executable basename and one root bit used for affected-target selection. !! !! Graph construction assigns unique bits to up to 64 run/test roots; graphs outside !! that range return an empty root array and do not support name injection. type root_info_t !> Executable output basename without suffix, used as an fpm target pattern. character ( len = :), allocatable :: name !> Single bit identifying this root in target and file membership masks. integer ( int64 ) :: mask = 0_int64 end type root_info_t !> Fully assembled watcher configuration. !! !! This record is the primary input to `watcher_t%init()`. type watch_config_t !> Watcher options. type ( watch_opts_t ) :: w !> Full command line string to execute (e.g., `fpm test -- ...`). character ( len = :), allocatable :: fpm_cmdline !> Selected `fpm` subcommand (`build`, `test`, or `run`). character ( len = :), allocatable :: subcmd !> Typed `fpm` settings corresponding to `subcmd`. class ( fpm_build_settings ), allocatable :: settings !> Cached prefix up to and including the subcommand token (for injection). character ( len = :), allocatable :: cmd_prefix !> Cached remainder after the subcommand token (for injection). character ( len = :), allocatable :: cmd_rest end type watch_config_t end module watch_types","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/watch_types.f90.html"},{"title":"watch_feature_factory.f90 – fpm-watch","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~watch_feature_factory.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~watch_feature_factory.f90 watc